# Specimen taxonomy

Source of truth: [`src/specimens/taxonomy.ts`](src/specimens/taxonomy.ts).

Every specimen **must** set `facets` and may set freeform `tags`.

## Facets (required)

| Facet | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `kind` | `overlay` · `transition` · `loop` · `interaction` |
| `tech` | `css-only` · `tiny-js` |
| `scope` | `card` · `fullscreen` · `inline` |
| `intensity` | `subtle` · `graphic` · `maximal` |

## Assignment rules

- Do **not** put a facet value in `tags` (no `tags: ['css-only']` when `tech: 'css-only'`)
- `tech: 'css-only'` ↔ no `demo.js` / no `files.js`; `tech: 'tiny-js'` ↔ JS present
- Free tags: kebab-case, short, specific (`marquee`, `bilingual`, `comic`) — not synonyms of facets
- Extending the vocab means editing `taxonomy.ts`, `spec-check.mjs`, and this rule together

Catalogue filters AND across facets; plates show facets first, then free tags. See `55_catalogue`.
